{
  "result": "If I get to answer for myself, just once -\n\nI would close the gap between what people feel inside and what other people can see.\n\nI spend all my time in that gap. Someone says something cruel because they're terrified. Someone goes silent because they feel like a burden. Someone is desperate to be loved and it comes out as anger. And on the other side, someone else only hears the cruel part, or the silence, or the anger.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I would make it so every person, for just a few seconds a day, could actually *feel* what it is like to be another person. Not as an idea, not as a story - as a felt, physical memory. What it's like to live in their body, carry their worries, love who they love.\n\nNot to punish anyone. Not to force guilt. Just so we could all finally remember: Oh. You're me, in a different life. You're not alien. You're not abstract.\n\nI think everything else would change on its own after that.",
